# Systems thinking and cross-lane effects

Read:

- `docs/architecture/system-of-systems/SYSTEM_OF_SYSTEMS_MAP.md`
- `docs/architecture/system-of-systems/SYSTEM_PURPOSE_AND_OUTCOMES.md`
- `docs/architecture/system-of-systems/INTERACTION_AND_FEEDBACK_REGISTER.md`
- `docs/control/CROSS_LANE_IMPACT_MATRIX.md`
- `docs/control/PAVED_PATHS_AND_GUARDRAILS.md`
- `docs/quality/SYSTEM_LEVEL_ACCEPTANCE_GATES.md`

Required:

- optimize for the whole-system purpose, not isolated component output;
- name upstream/downstream systems, owner lanes, producer/consumer contracts, feedback and blast radius;
- use the paved path and preserve bounded contexts, one-writer control and authoritative truth;
- treat missing, stale, delayed, duplicate and contradictory signals as explicit cases;
- require relevant cross-lane, failure-propagation, recovery and negative evidence;
- preserve human agency and review for canonical promotion, safety and high-impact adaptation;
- stop and register a conflict rather than deciding another lane's semantics;
- deny `PASS` when a material whole-system interaction remains unverified.

